msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:31
#: 3dfe216f8af148b8b1c5c9736be0b16b
msgid "Autopilot Connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:37
#: 614d2e73d2d84da9940b66bac7501256
msgid "Connect the solar panel, MPPT, battery and autopilot as shown above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:39
#: 696fe3d657754174afcff1e4157bbbb8
msgid "Once the solar panel provides more than 12V the board's LED should flash green.  Initially it may be easiest to connect a 4S or 6S battery to the board's VIN port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:42
#: c12cd0cb4f9e46f3a57a8eb38e7aabe5
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:44
#: 1ab540c9fd34414e8c22df3799b09352
msgid "Connect a ground station (e.g. Mission Planner) to the autopilot and set the following parameters and then reboot the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:46
#: 97d8b557646849a88d94c6983a7d7ce4
msgid ":ref:`BATT_MONITOR <BATT_MONITOR>` = 8 (DroneCAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:47
#: 0100a37e8b454cb482a7aee70f62ac77
msgid ":ref:`CAN_P1_DRIVER <CAN_P1_DRIVER>` = 1 (DroneCAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:48
#: fa68a74044c94c529b5e03256625a5ad
msgid ":ref:`BATT_OPTIONS<BATT_OPTIONS>` provides several options for MPPT enable and disable depending on autopilot events."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:50
#: dbb4361c41e1485582950f086f7ded6f
msgid "the MPPT can be manually turned on or off using an RC channel switch setup with its ``RCx_OPTION`` = 172."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:52
#: d7fdeb5082de4fa4b5cf66c110dd0719
msgid "Check the MPPT board's parameters by connecting through \"SLCAN\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:54
#: 1f1f269009e4475c898bd8560effa53d
msgid "Open Mission Planner's SETUP >> Optional Hardware >> UAVCAN(DroneCAN) page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:55
#: 0dadd935252b4888875ec76922c46c85
msgid "From the top right, select the COM port for the autopilot's SLCAN connection (normally one higher than the MAVLink COM port)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:56
#: a781123b90e249478db07e7549ec921e
msgid "Press the \"SLCan Mode CAN1\" button. The table should be filled in as shown below.  If this does not work try changing to the Config screen, connect over MAVLink and set :ref:`CAN_SLCAN_CPORT <CAN_SLCAN_CPORT>` = 1.  Return to SETUP >> Optional Hardware >> UAVCAN(DroneCAN) page and press the \"SLCan Mode CAN1\" button again"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:62
#: c16570684c2a451b82e481434cc63ede
msgid "Press the \"Menu\" button to view or change some of the MPPT's settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:64
#: 6d23254f72ca4383bac137f43439d444
msgid "mppt.vout_set configures the maximum voltage from the VOUT pin.  This should be equal to the battery's voltage when fully charged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:65
#: 4930fd810f8949cb916f5916176b2089
msgid "mppt.dcdc_en configures the board's startup behaviour.  If \"0\" the MPPT will not charge the battery until the autopilot is armed.  If \"1\" the MPPT will always attempt to charge the battery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:66
#: 8b10d3a9437d459a8d7f39a6f8cc460b
msgid "uavcan.node_id should normally be left at \"0\" to allow the autopilot to dynamically allocate the MPPT's DroneCAN node id but if multiple DroneCAN battery monitors or MPPTs are used you can manually set this to some value between 0 and 127 (e.g. \"50\") and then set :ref:`BATT_SERIAL_NUM <BATT_SERIAL_NUM>` to the same number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:69
#: 28298f236eaa4e1589e2e7ad0d33b258
msgid "Connecting more than one MPPT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:71
#: 0d794e5c9eb14d43b1fb8b3446cdf92d
msgid "More than one Packet Digital MPPT board can be connected in parallel to the same battery (but different solar panels) to increase the total current provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:73
#: 7e8de00280b14c1aaff4bec8d470dc3f
msgid "To allow the autopilot to connect to all the MPPTs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:75
#: d63bf7fc2f104b1fa9f466e5ddc79cc0
msgid "Enable one battery monitor per MPPT by setting :ref:`BATTx_MONITOR <BATT_MONITOR>` = 8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:76
#: 963229f09d1149f48c63ae2adf44ffeb
msgid "Use Mission Planner's SETUP >> Optional Hardware >> UAVCAN(DroneCAN) page's \"Menu\" button to manually configure the uavcan.node_id of each MPPT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:77
#: 7b9b01bb54a54f36ab13aceb81d942cf
msgid "set :ref:`BATTx_SERIAL_NUM <BATT_SERIAL_NUM>` to match the uavcan.node_ids set above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-packetdigital-mppt.rst:78
#: 6a762e1b841f4d71857f7886598dd317
msgid "You can sum all the MPPT currents using a \"SUM (10)\" power monitor type. See :ref:`common-power-module-configuration-in-mission-planner`."
msgstr ""

